OL,3,GNEWSATime capsule celebrates 100 years
OL,4,Aof Winnie-the-Pooh
OL,5,
OL,6,FA time capsule has been buried at a tea
OL,7,Froom in East Sussex to mark the 100th
OL,8,Fanniversary of the first
OL,9,FWinnie-the-Pooh book.
OL,11,FPooh Corner in Hartfield said the
OL,12,Fmemento to toast AA Milne's classic,
OL,13,Ffirst published on 14 October 1926,
OL,14,Fwill be reopened in 100 years.
OL,16,FThe capsule was filled with
OL,17,Fparaphernalia from across the year of
OL,18,Fcelebrations, which included books, a
OL,19,Frare Winnie-the-Pooh teapot, photos and
OL,20,Fletters to the bear from local
OL,21,Fschoolchildren.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,329,320,200,140,0,100
